# ex-vectors.golden — EX (MENU), Read direction
#
# ============================ SOURCE ============================
# Manual title as printed on cover:
#   "FTDX101MP / FTDX101D  CAT Operation Reference Manual"
#   (YAESU MUSEN CO., LTD.)
# Revision code as printed: 2308-L  (foot of final printed page, PDF 26)
# File consulted: docs/fixtures-private/manuals/ftdx101_cat_2308-L.pdf
#
# Position chart used:
#   Section heading "EX   MENU"
#   PRINTED page 9 (folio "9")  =  PDF page 10
#   (the EX section is the last on that page, directly below
#    "EU ENCODER UP" — heading confirmed in the rendered image)
# Chart direction the layout was read from: the READ position chart
#   (the row group labelled "Read").
# Menu addresses verified against: "Table 2 (MENU Chart)",
#   PRINTED pages 10, 11 and 12  =  PDF pages 11, 12 and 13.
#
# ---- DERIVATION METHOD -----------------------------------------
# Hand-derived from 400 dpi pdftoppm renders of PDF pages 10-13, cropped
# and enlarged 130-170% with ImageMagick and read as images. No text
# extraction. Position-header rows sit ABOVE the token rows they number.
#
# ---- FIELD MAP: READ direction (1-based positions) --------------
#   pos 1   : "E"   (literal, chart)
#   pos 2   : "X"   (literal, chart)
#   pos 3-4 : P1    (2 positions)  menu group   (legend: 01 - 05)
#   pos 5-6 : P2    (2 positions)  menu subgroup(legend: 01 - 07)
#   pos 7-8 : P3    (2 positions)  menu item    (legend: 01 - 23)
#   pos 9   : ";"   (terminator, chart)
#   => Read frame length 9 bytes including the ";".
#   The Read row's header runs 1..9, 10, nn, ** ; positions 10 onwards
#   are printed blank in the Read token row (P4 appears only in the Set
#   and Answer rows, where it runs from position 9 through "nn" with a
#   "~" continuation).
#
# ---- PARAMETER LEGEND as printed beside the EX charts -----------
#   P1  : 01 - 05
#   P2  : 01 - 07
#   P3  : 01 - 23
#   P4  : Parameter (See Table 2)
#
# ---- TABLE 2 ROWS CITED (each vector from a DIFFERENT menu group) --
#   ROW A  PRINTED page 10 (= PDF page 11)
#          P1 column : "01 (RADIO SETTING)"
#          P2 column : "01 (MODE SSB)"
#          P3 column : "10"
#          Function  : "TX BPF SEL"
#          P4 column : "0: 50 ~ 3050   1: 100 ~ 2900   2: 200 ~ 2800
#                       3: 300 ~ 2700   4: 400 ~ 2600"
#          Digits    : "1"
#
#   ROW B  PRINTED page 11 (= PDF page 12)
#          P1 column : "02 (CW SETTING)"
#          P2 column : "02 (KEYER)"
#          P3 column : "05"
#          Function  : "CW WEIGHT"
#          P4 column : "2.5 ~ 4.5 (P4 = 25 ~ 45)"
#          Digits    : "2"
#
#   ROW C  PRINTED page 12 (= PDF page 13)
#          P1 column : "04 (DISPLAY SETTING)"
#          P2 column : "02 (SCOPE)"
#          P3 column : "02"
#          Function  : "SCOPE CTR"
#          P4 column : "0: FILTER   1: CAR POINT"
#          Digits    : "1"
#
#   The three vectors therefore come from three different P1 menu groups
#   (RADIO SETTING, CW SETTING, DISPLAY SETTING), as required.
#
# ---- BYTE-BY-BYTE PROVENANCE -----------------------------------
# VECTOR 1  read_radio_ssb_tx_bpf_sel   "EX010110;"
#   pos 1-2 "EX"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid positions 1, 2.
#   pos 3-4 "01"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row A, P1 column "01
#                 (RADIO SETTING)"; inside legend range P1 01-05.
#   pos 5-6 "01"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row A, P2 column "01
#                 (MODE SSB)"; inside legend range P2 01-07.
#   pos 7-8 "10"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row A, P3 column "10"
#                 (TX BPF SEL); inside legend range P3 01-23.
#   pos 9   ";"   MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid terminator cell.
#
# VECTOR 2  read_cw_keyer_cw_weight     "EX020205;"
#   pos 1-2 "EX"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid positions 1, 2.
#   pos 3-4 "02"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row B, P1 "02 (CW SETTING)".
#   pos 5-6 "02"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row B, P2 "02 (KEYER)".
#   pos 7-8 "05"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row B, P3 "05" (CW WEIGHT).
#   pos 9   ";"   MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid terminator cell.
#
# VECTOR 3  read_display_scope_ctr      "EX040202;"
#   pos 1-2 "EX"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid positions 1, 2.
#   pos 3-4 "04"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row C, P1 "04
#                 (DISPLAY SETTING)".
#   pos 5-6 "02"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row C, P2 "02 (SCOPE)".
#   pos 7-8 "02"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Table 2 row C, P3 "02" (SCOPE CTR).
#   pos 9   ";"   MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid terminator cell.
#
# Every byte of all three frames is MANUAL-DOCUMENTED. The only free
# choices were WHICH rows to address, and those are cited above.
#
# INHERITED ASSUMPTIONS
#   A12 That P1/P2/P3 are written zero-padded to their two printed
#       positions (e.g. "05" rather than "5"). The legend prints the
#       ranges in two-digit form ("01 - 05" etc.) and the grid gives each
#       field two positions, but no padding rule is stated in words.
#       LIFTED BY: a real-radio EX Read whose Answer echoes P1/P2/P3 in
#       positions 3-8 — the echo shows the padding directly.
#   A13 That a Read request carries no P4 and terminates at position 9.
#       This is read off the Read grid (positions 10+ blank), but the
#       manual does not state it in prose.
#       LIFTED BY: sending "EX010110;" to a real radio and confirming a
#       well-formed Answer rather than a "?;" error reply.
#   A14 That every Table 2 row is individually addressable by EX Read on
#       both the FTDX101D and the FTDX101MP. Table 2 marks some P4 ranges
#       as model-specific (e.g. HF MAX POWER, printed page 12) but does
#       not say whether any row is absent on one model.
#       LIFTED BY: issuing each of these three Reads on each model and
#       comparing the replies.
#
# ---- ANOMALIES OBSERVED (recorded, not resolved) ---------------
#   N5  The EX legend gives "P1 : 01 - 05", but Table 2 as printed
#       contains only four P1 groups: 01 (RADIO SETTING), 02 (CW
#       SETTING), 03 (OPERATION SETTING) and 04 (DISPLAY SETTING). No
#       P1 = 05 group appears anywhere in Table 2 across printed pages
#       10-12. Recorded, not resolved. None of the vectors here uses 05.
#   N6  In the EX Set and Answer position charts the tenth header cell is
#       printed BLANK (the header row reads 1..9, [blank], nn, **),
#       whereas the Read chart's tenth header cell reads "10". The Set and
#       Answer token rows put a "~" continuation under that blank cell, so
#       the blank appears deliberate, but it is inconsistent with the
#       Read row. It affects no byte of these Read-direction vectors.
#
# ---- HARDWARE STATUS -------------------------------------------
#   UNVERIFIED. No frame here has been sent to, or captured from, a real
#   FTDX101MP or FTDX101D.
#
# Derivation date: 06/08/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document or web
# resource was consulted — only the single PDF named above.
#
read_radio_ssb_tx_bpf_sel	EX010110;
read_cw_keyer_cw_weight	EX020205;
read_display_scope_ctr	EX040202;
